            <CollapsibleNumericList
                givenID="SourceCode"
                givenNumber="2"
                givenHeader="Source Code"
                data="doc.license.sourceCode.header"
            >
                <p
                    class="my-2 text-LT_Primary dark:text-DT_Primary"
                    data-i18n="doc.license.sourceCode.paragraph_1"
                >
                    The "source code" for a work means the preferred form of the
                    work for making modifications to it. "Object code" means any
                    non-source form of a work. A "Standard Interface" means an
                    interface that either is an official standard defined by a
                    recognized standards body, or standard across a programming
                    language. The "Corresponding Source" for a work in object
                    code form means all the source code needed to generate,
                    install, and run the object code and to modify the work,
                    including scripts to control those activities.
                </p>
            </CollapsibleNumericList>

            <CollapsibleNumericList
                givenID="BasicPermissions"
                givenNumber="3"
                givenHeader="Basic Permissions"
                data="doc.license.basicPermissions.header"
            >
                <p
                    class="my-2 text-LT_Primary dark:text-DT_Primary"
                    data-i18n="doc.license.basicPermissions.paragraph_1"
                >
                    All rights granted under this License are granted for the
                    term of copyright on the Program, and are irrevocable
                    provided the stated conditions are met. This License
                    explicitly affirms your unlimited permission to run the
                    unmodified Program. The output from running a covered work
                    is covered by this License only if the output, given its
                    content, constitutes a covered work. You may make, run and
                    propagate covered works that you do not convey, without
                    conditions so long as your license otherwise remains in
                    force.
